BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Vidushi Ashwini Bhide Deshpande
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260423T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260423T200000
UID:vidushi-ashwini-bhide-deshpande-2026-04-23t20-00-00-04-00@agakhanmuseu
 m.org
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://images.agakhanmuseum.org/uploads/2026/03
 /Website-design-7-scaled-aspect-ratio-1600-1000-scaled.jpg?resize=1584%2C9
 90&gravity
DESCRIPTION:This performance has been postponed to April 23\, 2026. Your t
 icket and seat will automatically transfer to this date. Ticket holders wi
 ll receive an email with refund and credit options.\n\nPadma Shri awardee 
 Vidushi Ashwini Bhide Deshpande \, one of the foremost torchbearers of the
  Jaipur-Atrauli gharana\, returns to the stage for an evening of exquisite
  raag sangeet. Renowned for her intellectual depth\, emotional nuance\, an
 d masterful command of tradition\, she brings decades of performance\, sch
 olarship\, and celebrated recordings to this concert.\n\nShe is joined by 
 distinguished tabla artist Sanjay Deshpande \, a disciple of leading maest
 ros of the Delhi-Farukhabad tradition\, and harmonium accompanist Siddhesh
  Bicholkar \, whose sensitive musicianship has earned national recognition
 . Together\, they present a refined and immersive journey into Hindustani 
 classical music.
LOCATION:Nanji Family Foundation Auditorium\, Aga Khan Museum\, 77 Wynford
  Drive\, Toronto\, ON M3C 1K1
URL:https://agakhanmuseum.org/whats-on/vidushi-raag-mala/
X-SOURCE:Aga Khan Museum
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Unsolved Universe: Inside the Series
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260429T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260429T183000
UID:unsolved-universe-inside-the-series-2026-04-29t18-30-00-04-00@agakhanm
 useum.org
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://images.agakhanmuseum.org/uploads/2026/04
 /UU_KEY-ART_11-scaled-aspect-ratio-1600-1000-6-scaled.png?resize=1584%2C99
 0&gravity
DESCRIPTION:Join us for an evening of film and conversation that explores 
 how we come to understand the universe\, across time\, disciplines\, and w
 ays of knowing. Presented between International Astronomy Day and Space Da
 y\, this program brings together contemporary scientific storytelling and 
 the Museum’s broader engagement with the history of astronomy.\n\nThe ev
 ening features two episodes from Unsolved Universe : Pieces of the Past \,
  which follows a high-stakes mission to retrieve material from an asteroid
  in search of clues about the origins of life on Earth\, and Weird Worlds 
 \, which traces the discovery of planets beyond our solar system that chal
 lenge long-held assumptions about how planetary systems form.
LOCATION:Aga Khan Museum\, 77 Wynford Drive\, Toronto\, ON M3C 1K1
URL:https://agakhanmuseum.org/whats-on/unsolved-universe/
X-SOURCE:Aga Khan Museum
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Raaga Darshan
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260503T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260503T193000
UID:raaga-darshan-2026-05-03t19-30-00-04-00@agakhanmuseum.org
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://images.agakhanmuseum.org/uploads/2026/04
 /Raaga-Darshan_Poster-Banner-scaled-aspect-ratio-1600-1000.png?resize=1584
 %2C990&gravity
DESCRIPTION:Rooted in centuries of tradition\, this double-bill of Indian 
 classical music brings two distinguished performances together for one imm
 ersive experience. The artists showcase traditional compositions enriched 
 with spontaneous improvisation and intuitive interplay\, creating a dynami
 c dialogue between melody and rhythm.\n\nThe evening opens with legendary 
 tabla maestro Pandit Anindo Chatterjee in collaboration with sarode virtuo
 so Atish Mukhopadhyay\, presenting a deeply and expressive musical exchang
 e. Following this performance the acclaimed flautist Rakesh Chaurasia join
 s tabla prodigy Amit Kavthekar \, extending the journey with intuitive flu
 id interplay that builds on an already rich tapestry.\n\nMarketing Partner
 s
LOCATION:Ismaili Centre Toronto\, Aga Khan Museum\, 77 Wynford Drive\, Tor
 onto\, ON M3C 1K1
URL:https://agakhanmuseum.org/whats-on/raaga-darshan/
X-SOURCE:Aga Khan Museum
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Labyrinth Ensemble with Efrén López
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260509T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260509T200000
UID:labyrinth-ensemble-with-efr-n-l-pez-2026-05-09t20-00-00-04-00@agakhanm
 useum.org
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://images.agakhanmuseum.org/uploads/2026/03
 /Website-design-8-aspect-ratio-1600-1000.jpg?resize=1584%2C990&gravity
DESCRIPTION:Marking a new chapter of the Labyrinth Ensemble and a mileston
 e for the growth of modal music in Canada\, the ensemble project returns w
 ith a whole new cohort. 14 musicians start their four-year journey dedicat
 ed to studying and performing the many manifestations of modal music. With
  new instruments\, such as guzheng\, Hardanger fiddle\, qanun and microton
 al guitar\, each member of the group brings their own traditions to create
  a unique sound.\n\nJoining the ensemble from Valencia\, Spain\, guest mus
 ician Efrén López imparts 30+ years of modal exploration on hurdy gurdy 
 and a variety of lutes\, digging into European Medieval\, the Eastern Medi
 terranean\, the Middle East\, and Central Asian traditions.
LOCATION:Nanji Family Foundation Auditorium\, Aga Khan Museum\, 77 Wynford
  Drive\, Toronto\, ON M3C 1K1
URL:https://agakhanmuseum.org/whats-on/labyrinth-with-efren-lopez/
X-SOURCE:Aga Khan Museum
END:VEVENT
