BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Alexandru Sura and Vinay Desai
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260516T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260516T140000
UID:alexandru-sura-and-vinay-desai-2026-05-16t14-00-00-04-00@agakhanmuseum
 .org
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://images.agakhanmuseum.org/uploads/2026/04
 /Website-design-11-aspect-ratio-1600-1000-1.jpg?resize=1584%2C990&gravity
DESCRIPTION:Join Vinay Desai and Alexandru Sura for an engaging artist tal
 k and demonstration exploring the santoor and cimbalom. Through live examp
 les and conversation\, the artists will introduce the histories\, techniqu
 es\, and musical frameworks that shape their respective traditions\, from 
 Hindustani classical raag to Eastern European repertoire. Audiences will g
 ain insight into how these closely related instruments are played\, how th
 eir sounds are shaped\, and how each tradition approaches melody\, rhythm\
 , and improvisation.
LOCATION:Nanji Family Foundation Auditorium\, Aga Khan Museum\, 77 Wynford
  Drive\, Toronto\, ON M3C 1K1
URL:https://agakhanmuseum.org/whats-on/hammered-sura-desai-talk/
X-SOURCE:Aga Khan Museum
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Crossing Traditions: Cimbalom and Santoor in Dialogue
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260516T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260516T193000
UID:crossing-traditions-cimbalom-and-santoor-in-dialogue-2026-05-16t19-30-
 00-04-00@agakhanmuseum.org
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://images.agakhanmuseum.org/uploads/2026/04
 /Website-design-11-aspect-ratio-1600-1000.jpg?resize=1584%2C990&gravity
DESCRIPTION:This electrifying evening brings together the hammered-string 
 traditions of Europe and South Asia in a program unfolding in two immersiv
 e sets. First the Indian santoor\, then the European cimbalom\, echoing in
  conversation.\n\nExperience the captivating parallels between these instr
 uments as they move from intricate Indian rhythmic cycles to the bold\, ex
 pressive sounds of Eastern Europe. Virtuosic performances reveal both shar
 ed roots and distinct musical identities in a rich\, cross-cultural dialog
 ue.\n\nFeel the energy of a live cimbalom ensemble led by Alexandru Sura\,
  where dazzling technique meets deep emotion. Joined by violin\, kobza\, a
 nd double bass\, the group moves effortlessly from rapid-fire dances to ha
 unting\, lyrical melodies.
LOCATION:Nanji Family Foundation Auditorium\, Aga Khan Museum\, 77 Wynford
  Drive\, Toronto\, ON M3C 1K1
URL:https://agakhanmuseum.org/whats-on/hammered-cimbalom-santoor/
X-SOURCE:Aga Khan Museum
END:VEVENT
