BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Amir Amiri and Di Zhang
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260517T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260517T140000
UID:amir-amiri-and-di-zhang-2026-05-17t14-00-00-04-00@agakhanmuseum.org
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://images.agakhanmuseum.org/uploads/2026/04
 /Website-design-12-aspect-ratio-1600-1000-1.jpg?resize=1584%2C990&gravity
DESCRIPTION:In this interactive session\, Di Zhang and Amir Amiri offer a 
 closer look at the yangqin and santoor \, tracing their shared origins and
  distinct cultural evolutions. Through performance excerpts and discussion
 \, they will explore the instruments’ roles within Chinese and Persian m
 usical systems\, demonstrating techniques\, tonal possibilities\, and appr
 oaches to interpretation. This session offers a unique opportunity to expe
 rience the instruments up close while deepening understanding of their his
 tories and contemporary practices.
LOCATION:Nanji Family Foundation Auditorium\, Aga Khan Museum\, 77 Wynford
  Drive\, Toronto\, ON M3C 1K1
URL:https://agakhanmuseum.org/whats-on/hammered-amiri-zhang-talk/
X-SOURCE:Aga Khan Museum
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Silk Route Resonances: Santur and Yangqin Across Traditions
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260517T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260517T193000
UID:silk-route-resonances-santur-and-yangqin-across-traditions-2026-05-17t
 19-30-00-04-00@agakhanmuseum.org
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://images.agakhanmuseum.org/uploads/2026/04
 /Website-design-12-aspect-ratio-1600-1000.jpg?resize=1584%2C990&gravity
DESCRIPTION:Journey across cultures and centuries in this evocative evenin
 g exploring the Persian santur and the Chinese yangqin — two kindred ins
 truments shaped by distinct musical worlds.\n\nPresented in two immersive 
 sets\, the program begins with the yangqin before moving into the rich tra
 ditions of the Persian santur\, allowing each to unfold on its own terms. 
 From China’s diverse regional soundscapes to the intricate modal systems
  of Persian classical music\, the performance explores a vibrant blend of 
 connection\, evolution\, and exchange.\n\nTravel across China through the 
 shimmering tones of the yangqin. Beginning in Guangdong\, the music is gen
 tle and lyrical\, marked by refined phrasing and delicate melodies.
LOCATION:Nanji Family Foundation Auditorium\, Aga Khan Museum\, 77 Wynford
  Drive\, Toronto\, ON M3C 1K1
URL:https://agakhanmuseum.org/whats-on/hammered-santur-yangqin/
X-SOURCE:Aga Khan Museum
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Doors Open 2026
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260523T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260523T173000
UID:doors-open-2026-2026-05-23t10-00-00-04-00@agakhanmuseum.org
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://images.agakhanmuseum.org/uploads/2026/03
 /AKM-Doors-Open-Aly-Manji-2024-05-26-5069-scaled-aspect-ratio-1600-1000-sc
 aled.jpg?resize=1584%2C990&gravity
DESCRIPTION:Enjoy a weekend full of free tours\, family activities\, live 
 music\, and more as Doors Open returns to the Aga Khan Museum\, Aga Khan P
 ark\, and Ismaili Centre Toronto.\n\nFree | 10:30 am–4:30 pm\n\nImmerse 
 yourself in the Museum’s award-winning architecture\, Formal Gardens\, a
 nd Courtyard with a free tour. Plus\, enjoy a rare opportunity to step ins
 ide the Nanji Family Foundation Auditorium — one of the Museum’s true 
 architectural gems.
LOCATION:Aga Khan Museum\, 77 Wynford Drive\, Toronto\, ON M3C 1K1
URL:https://agakhanmuseum.org/whats-on/doors-open-2026/
X-SOURCE:Aga Khan Museum
END:VEVENT
